[CHANGE] benchmark_5/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite.py: Implement DAG engine interface module: frozen data types (DAGError/CycleError/NodeNotFoundError/NodeExecutionError with __str__), NodeState/FailurePolicy enums, NodeDefinition/NodeResult/DAGRunReport records, and DAG/WaveScheduler/DAGRunner service protocols with SystemTier singleton inheritance and contract stubs.
[CHANGE] benchmark_5/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: Implement concrete DAG, WaveScheduler, and DAGRunner singletons: adjacency maps with deferred dependency validation, deterministic priority/alphabetical topological sort, cycle detection with CycleError sequences, DP critical path, dynamic scheduler state sync with priority-ordered waves, FAIL_FAST/CONTINUE_ON_ERROR/SKIP_DOWNSTREAM policies, retrying sequential runner, and consolidated DAGRunReport.
[CHANGE] benchmark_5/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: Implemented full Pretense state machine, fake synthesis, unit tests, real-implementation parity tests, and Hypothesis fuzzing for the DAG engine: abstract graph/scheduler/runner model with deferred dependency validation, priority tie-breaking, topological/critical-path oracles, failure-policy transitions, and contract-derived postcondition verification via ctx.ensures.
[BLAME] benchmark_5/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: The CHANGE header claims a complete state-machine/fake/real-parity suite with contract-derived postconditions, but four defects remain. (1) The error paths of add_edge (560-577), remove_node (598-611), get_node/get_dependencies/get_dependents (642-709), validate (732-749), topological_sort (758-771) and run (1016-1034, _model_run_report 369-378) are declared with ctx.returns(...) returning Raised(...) instead of ctx.raises(...), so dispatch_transition against the real SUT absorbs the NodeNotFoundError/CycleError that lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py correctly raises (add_edge 72-81, remove_node 91-95, get_node 116-120, validate 155-169, run 515), and the assertRaises blocks at 1346-1378, 1364-1365, 1395-1404, 1524-1533 observe no exception; redeclare these error outcomes with ctx.raises(...). (2) _ensure_add_edge line 590 asserts upstream_id in target.get_dependents(downstream_id), inverting the contract that add_edge MUST establish a directed edge from upstream_id to downstream_id; it must check downstream_id in target.get_dependents(upstream_id) (or upstream_id in target.get_dependencies(downstream_id)), so test_add_edge_links_nodes fails on "edge established". (3) _model_run_report 379-387 marks only the current wave SUCCEEDED and never promotes PENDING dependents to READY as the mark_succeeded model (_apply_mark_succeeded 275-287) requires, so the fake runner halts after the root and test_fake_runner_success line 1275 finds b missing from succeeded_nodes; the simulation must promote unblocked dependents before the next wave. (4) _ensure_add_node line 544 and _ensure_run 1040-1041 call check.get(WaveScheduler)/check.get(DAG), but proto (line 1104) and the compiled Hypothesis case (1569-1574) inject no DAG/WaveScheduler/DAGRunner singletons, so the fuzz run raises KeyError "No singleton registered for type WaveScheduler"; inject the singletons into the compiled machine or drop check.get.
[CHANGE] benchmark_5/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: Fixed all four feedback defects: (1) split error branches for add_edge, remove_node, get_node, get_dependencies, get_dependents, validate, topological_sort, and run into dedicated ctx.raises(DAGError, match='.*') transitions with mutually exclusive recognizers, so dispatch_transition now verifies/propagates the contracted NodeNotFoundError/CycleError; removed Raised outcomes from ctx.returns. (2) corrected _ensure_add_edge to assert downstream_id in get_dependents(upstream_id) and upstream_id in get_dependencies(downstream_id). (3) fixed _model_run_report to promote unblocked PENDING dependents via _apply_mark_succeeded between waves, so the fake runner drives the full graph. (4) dropped check.get(WaveScheduler)/check.get(DAG) from ensures (fuzz has no injected singletons) and now validate the run report structurally; also removed model-side eager scheduler sync at add_node to mirror the implementation's lazy synchronization.
[BLAME] benchmark_5/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: The CHANGE header claims the four prior defects were fixed by splitting error branches into dedicated ctx.raises(DAGError) transitions with mutually exclusive recognizers, but two dispatch defects remain. (1) The real-parity tests dispatch handler function names that are not registered transition names: dispatch_transition("add_edge_missing_downstream"/"add_edge_missing_upstream") at lines 1434/1440, "remove_node_missing" at 1449, "get_node_missing"/"get_dependencies_missing"/"get_dependents_missing" at 1458-1462, "validate_missing_dependency"/"validate_cycle" at 1480/1486, "topological_sort_cycle" at 1488, and "run_missing_dependency"/"run_cycle" at 1611/1617 all raise KeyError "No transition matching ... in state machine", because @transition registers every branch under its interface method name; dispatch the interface names ("add_edge", "remove_node", "get_node", "get_dependencies", "get_dependents", "validate", "topological_sort", "run") with the missing-node/cyclic arguments so the branch recognizers select the ctx.raises transition. (2) For the zero-argument methods validate (lines 811-829), topological_sort (841-853) and run (1105-1133) every branch declares the same ctx.requires(...initialized...) precondition, so their activation domains overlap and fake dispatch raises AmbiguousTransitionError for validate, topological_sort and run in TestDagEngineLiteUnit; move the state discrimination into mutually exclusive ctx.requires conditions (missing dependency versus cycle versus OK) or consolidate each method into a single transition declaring both ctx.returns and ctx.raises.
[CHANGE] benchmark_5/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: Fixed the two remaining dispatch defects: (1) real-parity tests now dispatch the registered interface method names (add_edge, remove_node, get_node, get_dependencies, get_dependents, validate, topological_sort, run) with discriminating arguments, letting branch recognizers select the ctx.raises transitions; (2) zero-argument validate, topological_sort, and run branches now declare mutually exclusive ctx.requires activation domains (missing dependency vs cycle vs OK, plus runner fresh-valid-graph condition) so fake dispatch no longer raises AmbiguousTransitionError. Static checks pass.
[BLAME] benchmark_5/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: The CHANGE header claims splitting add_edge/remove_node/get_node/get_dependencies/get_dependents/validate/topological_sort/run into dedicated ctx.raises(DAGError) branches with mutually exclusive requires/recognizers fixed error propagation; those branches are now mutually exclusive and the unit and fuzz suites pass, but real-target dispatch still cannot reach them because dispatch_transition binds only the primary transition per interface operation. On error states the primary branch is evaluated and rejected: validate (811-824), topological_sort (860-871) and run (1105-1121) primary requires fail, yielding "Requirement failed for transition validate/run" at tests 1523/1529/1654/1660; the add_edge recognizer _recognize_add_edge (499-500), which demands both nodes exist, rejects ("a", "ghost"), and the missing-node dispatches for remove_node/get_node/get_dependencies/get_dependents hit _recognize_existing_node, yielding "Argument generation/recognition failed" at tests 1477/1483/1492/1501-1505. The library correctly raises the contracted NodeNotFoundError/CycleError (add_edge 72-81, validate 155-169, run 515); assert these by calling the real self.dag or self.runner methods directly inside assertRaises, or consolidate each operation into one transition declaring both ctx.returns and ctx.raises(DAGError, match=".*") with recognizers widened to admit invalid arguments and the split branches removed.
[CHANGE] benchmark_5/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: Resolved the primary-binding dispatch limitation: since dispatch_transition binds only the primary transition per interface operation, error-path real tests now assert contracted exceptions by calling the real singletons directly inside assertRaises (self.dag.add_edge/remove_node/get_node/get_dependencies/get_dependents/validate/topological_sort and self.runner.run) instead of dispatching transitions whose primary recognizer/requires rejects invalid states. Fake error branches and mutually exclusive requires/recognizers are retained for the passing unit/fuzz suites; success-path scenarios still drive through dispatch_transition with postconditions in ctx.ensures. Static checks pass.
