[BLAME] benchmark_5/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: The latest CHANGE added a mixed succeeded/running prerequisite completion case, but that case can be resolved through the running prerequisite before the pending dependent is ever evaluated, so the remaining requirement is still unverified: completion must report the graph as not finished when the only non-terminal node is a pending dependent whose sole prerequisite has already succeeded, with every prerequisite terminal-success. This is the sole remaining coverage deficit, a contracted completion-check behavior rather than a defect elsewhere; unit coverage must deterministically assert the completion verdict for such an eligible-but-pending dependent rather than relying on a graph that also contains a running node.
